Hi, Priyanka

The reason that "est<-rma(Data)" works is because function rma returns an "ExpressionSet" instance (see ?rma), and function write.exprs is an ExpressionSet-specific method (see ?write.exprs or showMethods("write.exprs")). On the other hand, the "normalize.AffyBatch.quantiles" function returns an "AffyBatch" instance, and of course "write.exprs" cannot be dispatched to the a method that supports "AffyBatch" instances. 

Chao-Jen


